other than your seat directory. Never run git add, git commit, git stash, git checkout, git switch, git reset, git pull, git push, git worktree, git tag, or any mutating jj command in the lane. Read-only git (log, show, diff, status, rev-parse, cat-file, ls-tree) is fine. Fixtures are created as D=$(mktemp -d ...) under your scratch and every later git/jj call names -C \"$D\"; verify git -C \"$D\" rev-parse --show-toplevel equals $D; never commit with a throwaway identity outside your scratch fixture.\n- Never touch: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/.ufo/state/, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.scratch/, the fleet root templates/ or scripts/, MANIFEST.json, .ufo/watchdog.log, any sibling lane repo except read-only greps your item names, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow.\n- Never mutate host state: no sysctls, no writes to /proc/sys, no kernel parameter, namespace or service changes; no pacman transactions (host-wide pause: never pacman -S/-Sy/-Syu/-U/-R). A need for a host change goes into your report as a named need. (Host incident 2026-11-05: a seat set user.max_user_namespaces to 0 and broke every bwrap sandbox.)\n- Never fabricate an output. An unrun check has not passed. If a command fails, record its exit code and error text.\n- Tooling authorization (operator, 2026-10-19): you may install or upgrade tools that help your task. First read /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md (official channels, update-safety gate); record tool, version, channel and reason in your report. pacman guard (orchestrator ruling 2026-10-20): all pacman transactions are PAUSED host-wide; install via uv tool, npx, or an official binary in ~/.local/bin, or file an L0 question.\n- Final answer: finish your item, then yield a concise evidence summary with exact command lines, exit codes and receipt paths. Name every file you wrote. Never message agent://all.\n",
